# Start
@novel
MOIRA: …

The scratching was getting worse. It was ringing in your ears. It didn’t help that Faust was still chattering up a storm. For someone who made a huge dramatic exit and said she was on her way out and everything…you can’t help but be a little grateful. 

Not that you’d ever admit to it. Even now, you’re trying as hard as you can to think about it in code. Admitting to this after your last real conversation was…

FAUST: Hey. There’s a major room left. If you can’t find it there, we should go.
MOIRA: …we, huh?
FAUST: You know what I mean.
MOIRA: Mm.

The crudely drawn map leads you to the master of the house’s bedroom.
